From: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:07:11 +0200
Subject: mptcp: prevent race between disconnect() and rtx
Git-commit: 85c580b0d8590520ae00a15c29e9fb9c99427a3e
Patch-mainline: v7.3-rc3
References: CVE-2026-97567 bsc#1283471

Sashiko noted that the two event can race, leading to inconsistent
status. Prevent the race using the synchronous timer stop operation.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Fixes: b29fcfb54cd7 ("mptcp: full disconnect implementation")
Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>
Reviewed-by: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260908-net-mptcp-misc-fixes-7-3-rc1-v2-6-df1de70348b6@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Pedro Falcato <pfalcato@suse.de>
---
 net/mptcp/protocol.c |   10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/mptcp/protocol.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/protocol.c
@@ -3133,6 +3133,7 @@ static void mptcp_copy_inaddrs(struct so
 
 static int mptcp_disconnect(struct sock *sk, int flags)
 {
+	struct inet_connection_sock *icsk = inet_csk(sk);
 	struct mptcp_sock *msk = mptcp_sk(sk);
 
 	/* We are on the fastopen error path. We can't call straight into the
@@ -3145,8 +3146,13 @@ static int mptcp_disconnect(struct sock
 	mptcp_check_listen_stop(sk);
 	inet_sk_state_store(sk, TCP_CLOSE);
 
-	mptcp_stop_timer(sk);
-	sk_stop_timer(sk, &sk->sk_timer);
+	/* The later subflow close can not kick again the tout timer,
+	 * as the msk is already in closed status.
+	 */
+	msk->timer_ival = TCP_RTO_MIN;
+	sk_stop_timer_sync(sk, &icsk->icsk_retransmit_timer);
+	icsk->icsk_mtup.probe_timestamp = 0;
+	sk_stop_timer_sync(sk, &sk->sk_timer);
 
 	if (msk->token)
 		mptcp_event(MPTCP_EVENT_CLOSED, msk, NULL, GFP_KERNEL);
